==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la}} {{term|pungens|lang=la}} (stem {{term||pungent-}}), present participle of {{term|pungo||to sting}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|pŭnjənt}}, {{IPA|/pɐnʤənt/}}, {{SAMPA|/pVndZ@nt/}}
* {{audio|en-us-pungent.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Having a [[strong]] [[odor]] that [[sting]]s the nose, said especially of [[acidic]] or [[spicy]] substances.
#: ''The lasagne included plenty of '''pungent''' garlic.''
#* '''1991''', [[w:Paul Chadwick|Paul Chadwick]], ''Concrete: American Christmas'', Dark Horse Books
#*: I can almost smell the fir scent… resinous, '''pungent'''.
# Having a [[sharp]] and [[stiff]] [[point]].
#: ''The critic gave a '''pungent''' review.''

====Derived terms====
* [[pungence]]
* [[pungently]]

